From d210b073ec246d6ef957849f406f83bc8d0c8234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:09:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plugins): a plugin prompt section can be larger than
 4,000 chars

A plugin system prompt section was cut at 4,000 characters, and 8,000 for all sections together, so project-memory could not show the notes up to the limit Jacob sets (8,000, and its own cap is 32,000).

plugins.max_section_chars (default 4000, never lower) is the largest max_chars a plugin may ask for when it registers a section. The aggregate budget is that value plus 4,000 (still 8,000 by default), and a persisted section is restored up to the same value. A section keeps its own max_chars, so plugins that ask for nothing stay at 4,000.
