 The agent also deduplicates file reads automatically — if the same file region is read twice and the file hasn't changed, a lightweight stub is returned instead of re-sending the content. This resets on context compression so the agent can re-read files after their content is summarized away.
 
+## Plugin prompt section size
+
+A plugin can add a section to the system prompt, at most 4,000 characters each and 8,000 together. A plugin that keeps more (such as project notes) asks for a larger `max_chars` when it registers, and Hermes grants it only up to `plugins.max_section_chars`:
+
+```yaml
+plugins:
+  max_section_chars: 12000   # default 4000 (the minimum); all sections together may use this plus 4000
+```
+
+A section over its own `max_chars` is skipped, as before. A value below 4,000, or one that is not an integer, is ignored; the highest allowed is 200,000. A section saved in a session's prompt is restored on resume only while it fits this limit.
+
 ## Tool Output Truncation Limits
 
 Three related caps control how much raw output a tool can return before Hermes truncates it:
